{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1329707-the-tumult-contract","id":1329707,"title":"The Tumult Contract","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-07T01:54:48-07:00","id":1329707,"title":"The Tumult Contract","content":"I was checking out this Contract recently, and I have a few questions about it:<br /> <br /> 1) Do you need to know the true name of the target before you can use this Contract? (Seems too limiting?) Or does the Contract effectively reveal the true name as you write it out? (Seems like too convenient a way to learn a true name, they're a big deal right? Admittedly I'm not entirely sure what a &quot;true name&quot; is supposed to <i>be</i> in a Changeling game, it is never really defined, so just going off of what I know of the general concept of a true name in myths/fantasy.)<br /> 2) It looks like you can essentially inflict 6 Conditions on someone if you get an Exceptional Success? Is that correct?<br /> 3) With 3 successes, if you have the Fairest Seeming benefit, you can inflict Swooning, Obsessed and Wanton on the target. Does that make this essentially the best seduction Contract that exists? It seems like a pretty heady mix!<br /> <br /> Overall, ignoring the question of how the true name thing works for a moment, this contract seems extremely strong! Being resisted rather than contested, it's not too hard to drown someone in 3+ Conditions whenever you use it. Might be stealing the thunder of some other Contracts a bit, considering you have several that have as effect &quot;inflict this one Condition on the target that can also be inflicted with Tumult&quot;, but Tumult puts a lot more of them down and lets you know what other Conditions affect the target as well. :O","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T03:42:55-07:00","id":1329862,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't know how the True Name thing works. <br /> <br /> I think Dream magic is the strongest seduction magic in the game or maybe Bedlam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 08-08-2019, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T11:07:39-07:00","id":1329932,"title":"","content":"Given how strong a Contract it is I\u2019d definitely say that you do in fact need to already know the target\u2019s true name for it to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T02:07:05-07:00","id":1330047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1329707-the-tumult-contract?p=1329932#post1329932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how strong a Contract it is I\u2019d definitely say that you do in fact need to already know the target\u2019s true name for it to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as an Ogre you can also give people -4 to all physical actions and -2 defense if you get 3 hits. Pretty wicked for such a versatile Contract! ^^<br /> <br /> I guess I can see how frequent use of Oneiromancy over time help an ongoing seduction focus pretty well, but talking more about the &quot;snap fingers, become adored for a time&quot; use, this Contract is certainly up there. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T13:01:25-07:00","id":1330292,"title":"","content":"How do you find someones true name? What counts as a true name for most people in CoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T17:20:58-07:00","id":1330322,"title":"","content":"I would personally say &quot;the name that they internally refer to themselves as&quot;, whatever that may be. (And any variant that they've internalized would also work: &quot;Dave&quot; and &quot;David&quot; would work the same, as long as he does indeed think of himself as Dave.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T17:56:21-07:00","id":1330327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7t7yiN_Z5eg\" data-code=\"7t7yiN_Z5eg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7t7yiN_Z5eg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Why does this forum require the least intuitive possible code for embedding videos? -_-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 08-10-2019, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T06:49:51-07:00","id":1331058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1329707-the-tumult-contract?p=1330047#post1330047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, as an Ogre you can also give people -4 to all physical actions and -2 defense if you get 3 hits. Pretty wicked for such a versatile Contract! ^^<br /> <br /> I guess I can see how frequent use of Oneiromancy over time help an ongoing seduction focus pretty well, but talking more about the &quot;snap fingers, become adored for a time&quot; use, this Contract is certainly up there. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Oneiromancy can go well beyond simple seduction, you can over time completely rewrite a persons personality, to make them into the perfect lover. But of course that would be beyond evil, so major clarity hit, because it's the sort of thing a True Fae would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 08-15-2019, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T08:43:54-07:00","id":1331073,"title":"","content":"CtL 2e really should have come with True Names rules. For humans at least I'd just use the name given at birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T00:57:43-07:00","id":1331180,"title":"","content":"You <i>could</i> have it be the same as their sympathetic name which is whatever most people called them when they were a kid, but IMO it\u2019s not really fitting to Changeling for forty year old Jameson\u2019s \u201ctrue\u201d name to be Jimmy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}